Here's how to implement this in .NET MAUI Shell:

## 1. Override `OnBackButtonPressed` in your page

```csharp
public partial class EditProductPage : ContentPage
{
    private bool _hasUnsavedChanges;

    protected override bool OnBackButtonPressed()
    {
        if (_hasUnsavedChanges)
        {
            // Fire-and-forget since the override is synchronous
            ShowUnsavedChangesDialog();
            return true; // Cancel navigation
        }
        return base.OnBackButtonPressed();
    }

    private async void ShowUnsavedChangesDialog()
    {
        bool leave = await DisplayAlert(
            "Unsaved Changes",
            "You have unsaved changes. Discard and go back?",
            "Discard", "Stay");

        if (leave)
            await Shell.Current.GoToAsync("..");
    }
}
```

## 2. Custom "Cancel" back button in XAML

```xml
<ContentPage xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/clr-namespace:YourNamespace"
             x:Class="YourNamespace.EditProductPage"
             Shell.BackButtonBehavior="{x:Static local:EditProductPage.CancelBackButton}">

    <!-- Or define inline: -->
    <Shell.BackButtonBehavior>
        <BackButtonBehavior Command="{Binding BackCommand}"
                           TextOverride="Cancel"
                           IconOverride="" />
    </Shell.BackButtonBehavior>

    <!-- Page content -->
</ContentPage>
```

## 3. ViewModel with BackCommand

```csharp
public partial class EditProductViewModel : ObservableObject
{
    [ObservableProperty]
    private bool _hasUnsavedChanges;

    [RelayCommand]
    private async Task Back()
    {
        if (HasUnsavedChanges)
        {
            bool leave = await Shell.Current.DisplayAlert(
                "Unsaved Changes",
                "You have unsaved changes. Discard and go back?",
                "Discard", "Stay");

            if (!leave) return;
        }

        await Shell.Current.GoToAsync("..");
    }
}
```

**Key points:**

- `OnBackButtonPressed` handles the hardware/gesture back (Android back button, swipe).
- `BackButtonBehavior` with `TextOverride="Cancel"` replaces the shell nav-bar arrow with a text button.
- Setting `Command` on `BackButtonBehavior` overrides the default navigation, so your dialog logic runs for the toolbar button too.
- Return `true` from `OnBackButtonPressed` to suppress default navigation while the async dialog is shown.
